### How many work orders exist before the replay, so the row COUNT can be the assertion rather than
### the status. A replay answered 201 while writing a second row is exactly the failure a
### status-only case would miss.
# @name CountBefore
## TEST-EXPECT-STATUS: [200]
GET {{fsBaseUrl}}/api/work_orders?limit=100&order=reference.asc
X-Alvo-Api-Key: {{keyDispatcherNorth}}

### The create a client sends, and never learns the outcome of
# @name FirstAttempt
## TEST-EXPECT-STATUS: [201]
POST {{fsBaseUrl}}/api/work_orders
X-Alvo-Api-Key: {{keyDispatcherNorth}}
Idempotency-Key: field-service-suite-replay-1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "tenant_id": "{{tenantNorth}}",
  "reference": "WO-6001",
  "title": "Retry me",
  "status": "scheduled",
  "priority": 2,
  "quoted_price": 500.00,
  "access_code": "RETRY",
  "customer_id": "{{CustomerAcmeId}}",
  "region_id": "{{RegionNorthId}}"
}

### The identical request again, byte for byte, as a client retries after a lost response
# @name Replay
## TEST-EXPECT-STATUS: [201]
POST {{fsBaseUrl}}/api/work_orders
X-Alvo-Api-Key: {{keyDispatcherNorth}}
Idempotency-Key: field-service-suite-replay-1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "tenant_id": "{{tenantNorth}}",
  "reference": "WO-6001",
  "title": "Retry me",
  "status": "scheduled",
  "priority": 2,
  "quoted_price": 500.00,
  "access_code": "RETRY",
  "customer_id": "{{CustomerAcmeId}}",
  "region_id": "{{RegionNorthId}}"
}

### The same key with a DIFFERENT body is a conflict, not a second create and not a silent replay
# @name SameKeyDifferentBody
## TEST-EXPECT-STATUS: [409]
POST {{fsBaseUrl}}/api/work_orders
X-Alvo-Api-Key: {{keyDispatcherNorth}}
Idempotency-Key: field-service-suite-replay-1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "tenant_id": "{{tenantNorth}}",
  "reference": "WO-6002",
  "title": "Different body, same key",
  "status": "scheduled",
  "priority": 2,
  "access_code": "RETRY",
  "customer_id": "{{CustomerAcmeId}}",
  "region_id": "{{RegionNorthId}}"
}

### A DIFFERENT key with the same body is a genuinely new create — the key scopes the record, and
### without this the case above could pass because the body was rejected for some other reason.
# @name DifferentKeySameShape
## TEST-EXPECT-STATUS: [201]
POST {{fsBaseUrl}}/api/work_orders
X-Alvo-Api-Key: {{keyDispatcherNorth}}
Idempotency-Key: field-service-suite-replay-2
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "tenant_id": "{{tenantNorth}}",
  "reference": "WO-6003",
  "title": "Retry me",
  "status": "scheduled",
  "priority": 2,
  "quoted_price": 500.00,
  "access_code": "RETRY",
  "customer_id": "{{CustomerAcmeId}}",
  "region_id": "{{RegionNorthId}}"
}

### An anonymous caller carrying a key is answered about the thing that actually stopped them.
###
### The port DOES refuse an anonymous idempotency key with a 422 — a record's identity is the key
### plus the caller, and every anonymous caller shares one reserved identity — but that refusal is
### unreachable here, and the reason is the design working: the endpoint resolves the operation's
### policy decision BEFORE it reads any header, so an anonymous caller on a tenant-scoped entity is
### told they are unauthorized rather than told to fix a header they were never going to get to use.
### Sending an agent to fix the wrong thing is precisely what that ordering exists to prevent.
# @name AnonymousKey
## TEST-EXPECT-STATUS: [403]
POST {{fsBaseUrl}}/api/work_orders
Idempotency-Key: field-service-suite-anonymous
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "tenant_id": "{{tenantNorth}}",
  "reference": "WO-6004",
  "title": "Anonymous",
  "status": "scheduled",
  "priority": 2,
  "access_code": "RETRY",
  "customer_id": "{{CustomerAcmeId}}",
  "region_id": "{{RegionNorthId}}"
}

### The state of the world: two new rows for two distinct keys, and nothing for the replay or the conflict
# @name CountAfter
## TEST-EXPECT-STATUS: [200]
GET {{fsBaseUrl}}/api/work_orders?limit=100&order=reference.asc
X-Alvo-Api-Key: {{keyDispatcherNorth}}

### And the replayed reference names exactly one row, not two
# @name RowsForTheReplayedReference
## TEST-EXPECT-STATUS: [200]
GET {{fsBaseUrl}}/api/work_orders?reference=eq.WO-6001&limit=100
X-Alvo-Api-Key: {{keyDispatcherNorth}}

### The two rows this case created are removed again, so every later group measures the seeded seven
### rather than an inherited leftover. Asserted below, not assumed.
# @name RemoveReplayedRow
## TEST-EXPECT-STATUS: [204]
DELETE {{fsBaseUrl}}/api/work_orders/{{FirstAttempt.response.body.$.id}}
X-Alvo-Api-Key: {{keyDispatcherNorth}}

